Description:
    Scaffolds the Mixin output-polling foundation: the receipt and cursor
    tables with models, and an example processor under app/mixin/processors.
    Receipts deduplicate every observed output (inbound or outbound); the
    cursor survives poller restarts; processors are selected by predicate and
    run in the job queue.

    Start polling with the rake task (bots default to MixinBot's global
    credentials; pass a registered bot name for multi-bot apps):

        rails mixin_bot:poller            # default bot
        rails mixin_bot:poller[shop]      # registered bot :shop

Example:
    rails generate mixin_bot:outputs

    This will create:
        db/migrate/xxx_create_mixin_outputs.rb
        db/migrate/xxx_create_mixin_poller_cursors.rb
        app/models/mixin_output.rb
        app/models/mixin_poller_cursor.rb
        app/mixin/processors/deposit_processor.rb

    Run `rails db:migrate` afterwards, and make sure a job backend
    (e.g. Solid Queue) is running for processor jobs.
